return A.c(A.n9(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Contract Rummy How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tag-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #d6a633;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tag-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Contract Rummy How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Seven deals, seven contracts: lay down what each deal asks for, then go out.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Each of the seven deals has a contract you must lay down before you can lay off or go out. When a player goes out, everyone else is charged for the cards left in their hand. After the seventh deal, the lowest total wins.</p>\n      <ol>\n        <li>Two sets</li>\n        <li>A set and a run</li>\n        <li>Two runs</li>\n        <li>Three sets</li>\n        <li>Two sets and a run</li>\n        <li>A set and two runs</li>\n        <li>Three runs</li>\n      </ol>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Number of players: </strong>2 to 6.</li>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>each player has a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch any other player between Human and Robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. Cards and Melds</h3>\n      <p>The game uses two decks and four jokers. Each player gets 10 cards in the first three deals and 12 after that.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Set: </strong>3 or more cards of the same rank.</li>\n        <li><strong>Run: </strong>4 or more cards of one suit in a row. Aces are low (A-2-3-4) or high (J-Q-K-A), but a run cannot go round the corner.</li>\n        <li><strong>Jokers </strong>are wild and can stand in for any card, but every meld needs at least 2 natural cards.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Your Turn</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>take the top card of the stock or the top discard.</li>\n        <li><strong>Go down: </strong>tap the cards of one meld and press Meld. Your melds only count once they make the whole contract; until then you can press Take Back. You cannot discard with a contract half laid down.</li>\n        <li><strong>Lay off: </strong>once you are down, add cards to any meld on the table, on later turns too.</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard: </strong>end your turn with one card on the discard pile.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>If the stock runs out, the discards are shuffled into a new stock.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Scoring</h3>\n      <p>When a player has no cards left, the deal ends. Everyone else scores the cards left in their hand: 2s to 9s 5, 10s and face cards 10, aces 15, jokers 25. Low scores are good.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your draw, your melds or your discard. The recommended button or cards are outlined in white. Robots use the same advice: they take a discard only when it is a joker or completes their contract, go down as soon as they can, lay off natural cards first, and throw away the card that helps their contract least.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each player\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tag-room-how-to-play 8 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Contract Rummy is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tag_contract_rummy_engine"),$async$KP)
