return A.c(A.n9(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Euchre How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tag-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #d6a633;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tag-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Euchre How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Four players, two partnerships, five tricks a hand.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>You and your partner, who sits across from you, play against the other two players. Name trump and take at least three of the five tricks, or stop the other team from doing it. The first team to reach the target score wins.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>Player 1 (South) is you. Your partner is Player 3 (North). Players 2 and 4 (West and East) are your opponents. Any player except Player 1 can be a robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Points to win: </strong>5, 7 or 10.</li>\n        <li><strong>Stick the dealer: </strong>When everyone passes twice, the dealer must name trump. When this is off, the cards are thrown in and the next player deals.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n        <li><strong>Robot skill: </strong>Beginner, Intermediate or Expert. All robots play at the same level.</li>\n        <li><strong>Show hints: </strong>On or off. When it is off, there is no Hint button and no recommended button or card.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. The Cards</h3>\n      <p>Euchre uses 24 cards: the 9, 10, jack, queen, king and ace of each suit. Once trump is named, the highest trump is the jack of trump (the right bower), then the other jack of the same color (the left bower), which counts as a trump, then the ace, king, queen, 10 and 9 of trump.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Naming Trump</h3>\n      <p>Each player gets five cards and one card is turned up. Starting to the dealer\'s left, each player can <strong>Order Up</strong> that card\'s suit as trump or <strong>Pass</strong>. If someone orders it up, the dealer picks up the card and throws one away.</p>\n      <p>If everyone passes, the card is turned down, and each player in turn can name any other suit or pass.</p>\n      <p>The player who names trump can <strong>Go Alone</strong>. Their partner sits out the hand, and taking all five tricks scores more.</p>\n      <p>If the dealer\'s partner orders up and goes alone, the dealer sits out, and nobody picks up the turned card.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Playing the Tricks</h3>\n      <p>The player to the dealer\'s left leads the first trick. Everyone must follow the suit that was led if they can; remember the left bower belongs to the trump suit. The highest trump wins the trick, or the highest card of the suit led if no trump was played. The winner leads the next trick.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Scoring</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>3 or 4 tricks: </strong>the team that named trump scores 1 point.</li>\n        <li><strong>All 5 tricks: </strong>2 points, or 4 points when going alone.</li>\n        <li><strong>Fewer than 3 tricks: </strong>the team that named trump is euchred, and the other team scores 2 points.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your bid, discard or play. The recommended button or card is outlined in white. Hints always give the Expert robot\'s advice, with its reasons and, when they help, its chances. Beginner robots name trump when their hand is strong enough, lead aces and trump, and play low when their partner is winning the trick. Intermediate and Expert robots work out many possible ways the hidden cards can be split, and they play to win the game, not only the hand.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>8. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with the teams and the final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tag-room-how-to-play 9 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Euchre is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tag_euchre_engine"),$async$JV)
