s=3
return A.c(A.n9(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Gin Rummy How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tag-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #d6a633;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tag-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Gin Rummy How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Build melds in your hand, cut your deadwood, and knock before your opponent does.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Gin Rummy is for two players. Arrange your 10 cards into sets (3 or 4 of a rank) and runs (3 or more of a suit in a row, aces low). Cards that are not in a meld are deadwood: face cards 10, aces 1, other cards their number. Get your deadwood low and knock, or get it to nothing and go gin. The first player to reach the target score wins the game.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>two, each with a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch Player 2 between Human and Robot. If both are people, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Points to win: </strong>50, 100 or 150.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. Your Turn</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>take the top card of the stock, or the top card of the discard pile.</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard: </strong>tap a card and press Discard. You cannot throw back the card you just took from the discard pile.</li>\n        <li><strong>Knock: </strong>if your deadwood after the discard is 10 or less, press Knock instead. With no deadwood at all, the button says Gin.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Your hand is always arranged for you: melds first, outlined in blue, then your deadwood. The deadwood total shows above your cards.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Knocking and Scoring</h3>\n      <p>When a player knocks, the other player lays off any deadwood cards that fit the knocker\'s melds (not after gin), and both deadwood totals are compared.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Knock: </strong>the knocker scores the difference in deadwood.</li>\n        <li><strong>Undercut: </strong>if the other player has as little deadwood or less, they score the difference plus 25.</li>\n        <li><strong>Gin: </strong>the player going gin scores the other player\'s deadwood plus 25.</li>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>if the stock gets down to two cards without a knock, the hand is a draw.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>The loser of each hand deals the next one.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. End of the Game</h3>\n      <p>When a player reaches the target, they get a 100-point game bonus, and each player gets 25 for every hand they won.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your draw and your discard. The recommended button or card is outlined in white. Robots use the same advice: they take the discard only when it makes a meld, throw the card that leaves the least deadwood, and knock as soon as they can.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each player\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tag-room-how-to-play 8 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Gin Rummy is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tag_gin_rummy_engine"),$async$KZ)
