return A.c(A.n9(m,"how_to_play",'<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang="en">\n<head>\n  <meta charset="UTF-8">\n  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">\n  <title>T-G-Apps Indian Rummy How to Play</title>\n  <style>\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 16px;\n      background: #f6f1e4;\n      color: #111827;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      line-height: 1.45;\n    }\n\n    .tag-policy-page {\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 900px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n    }\n\n    .hero,\n    .card {\n      display: block;\n      width: auto;\n      margin: 0 0 14px 0;\n      padding: 14px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n      background: #ffffff;\n      border: 1px solid #d6a633;\n    }\n\n    .hero {\n      background: #063a25;\n      color: #ffffff;\n    }\n\n    .badge {\n      display: none;\n    }\n\n    h1, h2, h3 {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n      color: #063a25;\n    }\n\n    .hero h1,\n    .hero h2 {\n      color: #ffd966;\n    }\n\n    p {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n    }\n\n    ul {\n      margin: 0 0 10px 22px;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    li {\n      margin-bottom: 5px;\n    }\n\n    a {\n      color: #0b63ce;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n\n    .footer {\n      text-align: center;\n      color: #ffffff;\n      background: #063a25;\n      padding: 12px;\n      border-radius: 12px;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <div class="tag-policy-page">\n    <section class="hero">\n      <h1>T-G-Apps LLC</h1>\n      <h2>T-G-Apps Indian Rummy How to Play</h2>\n      <p class="subtitle">Arrange all 13 cards into sequences and sets, with a pure sequence, and declare before anyone else.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>1. Goal</h3>\n      <p>Indian Rummy is played with 13 cards. Be the first to arrange your whole hand into sequences and sets and declare. This is pool rummy: the other players score points for the cards they could not meld, and a player who reaches the limit (101 or 201) is out. The last player left wins.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>2. Setup Options</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Number of players: </strong>2 to 6.</li>\n        <li><strong>Players: </strong>each player has a name and a type. Player 1 is always a person; tap the Type button to switch any other player between Human and Robot. If more than one person plays, pass the phone when the game asks you to.</li>\n        <li><strong>Out at: </strong>101, or 201 for a longer game.</li>\n        <li><strong>Music: </strong>Background music on or off, and its volume.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>3. Cards and Wild Cards</h3>\n      <p>The game uses two decks and two printed jokers. After the deal, one card is cut and shown face up: every card of its rank is wild for the hand, and so are the printed jokers. If the cut card is a joker, aces are wild. Wild cards are marked W in your hand.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Pure sequence: </strong>3 or more cards of one suit in a row with no wild card standing in, such as 4-5-6 of hearts. Aces are low (A-2-3) or high (Q-K-A).</li>\n        <li><strong>Sequence: </strong>the same, with wild cards filling gaps.</li>\n        <li><strong>Set: </strong>3 or 4 cards of one rank in different suits, wild cards allowed.</li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>4. Your Turn</h3>\n      <ul>\n        <li><strong>Draw: </strong>take the top card of the stock, or the top discard. A wild card on the discard pile cannot be taken.</li>\n        <li><strong>Discard or declare: </strong>tap a card and press Discard. If all your other 13 cards are in sequences and sets, with at least two sequences and one of them pure, press Declare instead.</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Your hand is arranged for you: pure sequences outlined in light blue, other sequences in purple, sets in green, then the cards that do not fit.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>5. Scoring</h3>\n      <p>The player who declares scores nothing. Every other player with two sequences, one of them pure, scores only the cards they could not meld; without them, every card counts. Aces and face cards count 10, other cards their number, wild cards nothing, and no one scores more than 80 in a hand. Low scores are good.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>6. Hints and Robots</h3>\n      <p>Press Hint for advice on your draw and your discard. The recommended button or card is outlined in white. Robots use the same advice: they take a discard when it fits their sequences or sets, keep wild cards, throw away the card that fits least, and declare as soon as they can.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>7. Games History</h3>\n      <p>Every finished game is saved with each player\'s final score. Games History lists the newest games first.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <!-- tag-room-how-to-play 8 -->\n\n    <section class="card">\n      <h3>Responsible Play</h3>\n      <p>T-G-Apps Indian Rummy is an entertainment game. It does not offer real-money gambling, prizes, wagers or cash-out functionality.</p>\n    </section>\n\n    <p class="footer">\xa9 2026 T-G-Apps LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n',"tag_indian_rummy_engine"),$async$KK)
